{
 "id": "PV-SS14",
 "title": "A grate on a grade with the moving-water law (F21), on two gutter shapes",
 "category": "integration",
 "process": "the same gutter and grate as PV-SS13, with the coupler option capture: hec22 (drainage.js grateCapture), and a second gutter shape not seen before",
 "module": "street/score.mjs",
 "executor": "node (CPU surface solver) and browser (GPU); raw measurements in street/raw/, scored by run.mjs",
 "equations": [
  "gutter (FHWA HEC-22 Eq. 4-2): Q = (0.376 / n) Sx^1.67 SL^0.5 T^2.67; depth at the kerb T Sx; mean depth over the first metre Sx (T - 0.5)",
  "grate on a grade (Eq. 4-16, 4-19, 4-20): frontal share Eo = 1 - (1 - W/T)^2.67, side interception Rs = 1 / (1 + 0.0828 V^1.8 / (Sx L^2.3)), efficiency E = Eo + Rs (1 - Eo), with all the frontal flow taken (velocities below splash-over)",
  "flow reaching the grate at steady state: rain x street width x distance from the top"
 ],
 "initialConditions": "dry",
 "boundaryConditions": "kerb and the other three sides: walls, except the foot of the street, a free-outfall edge; the grate sits on a 0.45 m pipe to a free outfall that never limits it",
 "geometry": "a: the PV-SS13 street (half street 100 x 8 m, Sx 2 %, n 0.016, SL 1, 2, 4 %, rain 50, 100, 200 mm/h). b and c: a second shape, half street 100 x 10 m, Sx 3 %, n 0.015, SL 0.5, 1.5, 3 %, rain 60 and 150 mm/h; b with the capture law, c without it (the control). One grate in the kerb cell at 75.5 m, 0.6 x 0.9 m for HEC-22 and for the capture law; 1 m cells",
 "parameters": {
